AUPRG / AP_norm are baseline-anchored skill scores (random -> 0 at any
prevalence), NOT prevalence-invariant; AUROC is the only invariant column.
[1] AUPR is the vendored benchmark's trapezoidal auc(recall, precision)
    (the auc(recall, precision) call in cal_metrics), kept for comparability with
    published SLMGAE/SLGNN/NSF4SL tables. It linearly interpolates between
    PR points, which no classifier achieves, and rewards ties: a CONSTANT
    score matrix scores exactly (1+baseline)/2 — i.e. the `baseline`
    column of this very table determines it, and on every CV here that
    lands near 0.585, above most real models. NOT hard-coded: an earlier
    footnote quoted 0.5786, which was the value under the pre-2026-08-10
    fold set and silently went stale when the label rule changed.
    Report AP (average precision), which gives a constant predictor exactly
    `baseline`.
[2] maxF1 is the MAXIMUM F1 over the PR curve, i.e. an oracle threshold
    chosen against the test labels (the max-F1 expression in cal_metrics).
    It is applied identically to every model, but it is not an operating
    point any deployed model could pick.
