All models rank against the SAME shared gene universe
(sl_comparison/folds/genes.txt) on the SAME folds, siamese_sl included
(every siamese config.json carries folds_dir=../sl_comparison/folds).
The columns differ only in how they are NORMALISED:
  R@k       hits@k / #relevant. Correct as published - prefer these.
  NDCG@k    vendored: IDCG taken over the model's OWN top-100, so IDCG =
            min(k, hits-in-top-100) instead of min(k, #relevant)
            (cal_metrics' ndcg_score call, handed y_bool over the model's
            own top-100). Inflated.
  NDCG@kc   same ranking, IDCG from the true #relevant. Corrected.
  MAP@k     vendored: AP divided by hits-in-top-k rather than
            min(k, #relevant) (calculate_AP_at_k). Inflated more
            than NDCG.
  MAP@kc    same ranking, divided by min(k, #relevant). Corrected.
  P@10      vendored: hits/min(k, #relevant) - a second copy of R@k
            whenever #relevant <= k (cal_metrics' precision_k block),
            not precision.
  P@10t     true hits/k.
The corrections shrink every score and shrink the WEAKEST retriever most;
on the 2026-08-06 run they reordered no cell. See retrieval_metrics.py.
degen-rows = fraction of scored test genes whose score row is CONSTANT.
  Those genes' @k values are an arbitrary tie-break, not model output, and
  do not reproduce across numpy versions. Any row with a non-trivial
  degen-rows figure has a retrieval column that should not be published.
=========================================================================================================================================================================================================================

